<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE X3D PUBLIC "ISO//Web3D//DTD X3D 3.3//EN" "http://www.web3d.org/specifications/x3d-3.3.dtd">
<X3D profile='Interchange' version='3.3'>
  <head>
    <meta name='description' content='Functional smoke test (duktape): a Script initialize() gets Browser.currentScene (an X3DExecutionContext), creates six Group nodes with ec.createNode, and registers each with ec.updateNamedNode. This exercises the SAI createNode + updateNamedNode append path end to end. Pass: DUK_DEFNAMES_START, DUK_DEFNAMES_UPDATE_1..6 and DUK_DEFNAMES_DONE all print, with no crash and no AddressSanitizer report. NOTE: this is NOT a memory-safety regression guard. updateNamedNode has a latent DEF-name Vector element-size bug (it lazily creates the list with newVector(struct brotoDefpair*,4) instead of struct brotoDefpair), but createNewX3DNode always pre-creates a correctly-sized __DEFnames via add_empty_proto_vectors before any script runs, so the buggy branch is not reachable from script and this fixture passes with and without the fix.'/>
  </head>
  <Scene>
    <Background skyColor='0.1 0.1 0.2'/>
    <Viewpoint position='0 0 6' description='front'/>
    <Shape>
      <Appearance><Material diffuseColor='0 1 0'/></Appearance>
      <Box size='1.5 1.5 1.5'/>
    </Shape>
    <Script>
<![CDATA[javascript:
function initialize() {
	print('DUK_DEFNAMES_START');
	var ec = Browser.currentScene;
	for (var i = 1; i <= 6; i++) {
		var n = ec.createNode('Group');
		ec.updateNamedNode('defname_' + i, n);
		print('DUK_DEFNAMES_UPDATE_' + i);
	}
	print('DUK_DEFNAMES_DONE');
}
]]>
    </Script>
  </Scene>
</X3D>
